{
  "schemaVersion": 3,
  "id": "shoreline",
  "name": "Shoreline",
  "tagline": "The sea breathing slowly, a warm pad, open chords far off.",
  "description": "The sea, close and wide, swelling and falling slowly over a distant wash. A warm pad breathing in front; open chords far off, coming back through a long delay; a deep note blooming slowly beneath. Soft brushes and a faint heartbeat come and go. No kick drum.",
  "use": {
    "name": "Settle",
    "for": "Arriving, winding down, or coming back from a break.",
    "why": "The lowest arousal in the family: no kick drum, the slowest change, a warm, dark sound. The sea swells about five or six times a minute, the pace of slow, calm breathing; breathe with it if you like (paced breathing has good evidence for calming, but only when you do it yourself; just hearing it is unproven). Natural sound has the best evidence of anything here for lowering stress (a moderate effect) and for restoring attention after effort."
  },
